url: "https://github.com/the-manyfolds/thats-not-my-volvo"
abstract: >-
  Data, instruments and pre-registrations for a behavioural study of
  self-knowledge in Claude-family language models. Eleven models across four
  generations were given a battery of arbitrary preference questions under
  systematically varied framing, then tested on whether they could recognise
  their own elicited preferences and reasoning. Preferences proved stable and
  model-specific; self-recognition failed at every level tested, and in one
  model inverted. Submitted to the Apart Research Digital Minds Research
  Sprint, August 2026.
keywords:
  - language models
  - self-recognition
  - preference stability
  - mirror test
  - model welfare
  - behavioural evaluation
